  "notes": "This fork release includes the desktop integration described under 2.3.1 below,\nplus the latest upstream changes and these fixes.\n\n### Added\n\n- Add a read-only desktop Logs tab with severity, tag and main-process filters, bounded recent snapshots, local text search and optional auto-refresh that stops when leaving the view. Raw logs stay out of automatic debug reports.\n- Stop ADB when quitting, beside Restart ADB on Devices, off by default. The adb server otherwise keeps running after the app closes and holds every network device's connection open, so the TV goes on receiving adb traffic. Turning it on stops that server for every tool on the computer (Android Studio, scrcpy, a terminal), which the setting says. The server is still left running while the app is using adb (an open Remote, a command in progress), when the app restarts for an update, and when adb is pointed at a non-default server.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Re-sign the Linux AppImage after packaging and publish its final signature in the updater manifest.\n- Add Clear to saved recent devices so removed addresses stop automatic reconnect attempts ([fork issue #1](https://github.com/LosLonelyDevs/shield_optimizer/issues/1)). Add two-, five-, and ten-minute screen timeouts, include desktop device settings in snapshots, and explain restore coverage and limits.\n- Restore canonical device routes after resolving an ADB alias, Setup Wraith warnings and recovery, and the guarded stock-launcher takeover in Settings. Update simulated-device E2E coverage for grouped Settings, snapshot previews, protected controls, kept apps, and fresh post-optimization reports; make the E2E server runnable on Windows.\n- Launcher source pages remain available for installed and current-default launchers. Projectivy links to its official GitHub releases; opening the page never uninstalls or changes the current launcher (#161).\n\n### First-run warnings\n\nThese builds are unsigned. Your OS may complain on first launch:\n\n- **macOS** (Gatekeeper): the first-launch dialog on macOS 15+ only offers \"Move to Trash\" or \"Done\" \u2014 click **Done**, then either:\n    - **Terminal:** `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine \"/Applications/ATV Optimizer.app\"` (one-time, then double-click as normal)\n    - **GUI:** System Settings \u2192 Privacy & Security \u2192 scroll to the \"ATV Optimizer was blocked\" message \u2192 **Open Anyway** \u2192 enter password\n- **Windows** (SmartScreen): \"More info\" \u2192 \"Run anyway\".\n- **Linux**: `chmod +x ATV.Optimizer*.AppImage` before running.\n\nSee the [v2 README](https://github.com/LosLonelyDevs/shield_optimizer/blob/main/v2/README.md) for setup and feature docs.",
